{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792125626,"nonce":"vtCMDKl4bNr5NBfgq2kqrQhe1Hg=","message":"Decision: redirect hops use a streamed GET closed after the headers (new FetchContext.get_hop), not HEAD. Reason: some redirectors and ATSs answer HEAD with 405/404 or a different Location, and one GET per hop needs no fallback; a 3xx with Location is closed unread, every other response (2xx, 4xx, 3xx without Location) is read in full inside the concurrency slots, so all walk checks are unchanged. Decision: such a hop logs fetch_log bytes=0 and content_hash NULL. Reason: no body was stored; a NULL hash also keeps it out of conditional-request lookups. Decision: reverify uses get_hop too. Reason: same one-hop redirect read, body only where it checks the closed-posting text.","files":null}]}